# winemac: Post IME updates directly from the Cocoa main thread.
# https://gitlab.winehq.org/wine/wine/-/merge_requests/12164 state=closed
# This works by first allowing `WINE_IME_POST_UPDATE` to post cross-thread, and then refactoring winemac in such a way to directly post and avoid using `IM_SET_TEXT`.

I also took the liberty of consolidating all IME-related functions into their own file instead of having them split up in keyboard.c and event.c (where the latter doesn't make sense anymore at all after this series).

The `PsGetCurrentThreadId()` related TODO can also be removed once !9503 is in. All other uses that require Windows headers are still working via C exports, similar to how it was handled previously.
